{
  "dom_id": "step-t8284",
  "name": "The Standard Normal Cumulative Distribution Function",
  "problem": "The **cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution** is defined by\n\n$$\n\\Phi(z) = P(Z \\leq z),\n$$\n\nwhere $P(Z \\leq z)$ denotes the probability that $Z\\sim N(0,1)$ is less than some fixed value $z.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/43b5489abd69bd4bb9558dcb0850bab2e19a9c9794ec093f73c5e163b46bb402.png)\n\nFor example, using the result we saw earlier, \n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq 1) = \\Phi(1)  = 0.8413\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/8a2c99700ce2c2b7d6808da06c83570da25ee0107ad5d796f637b7dd1079c90c.png)\n\nThe symbol $\\Phi$ is called \"Phi\" and rhymes with \"fly.\"\n\nWhen we need to find values of $\\Phi(z),$ we often use a lookup table, like the one shown below:\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.01 \\,$ | $\\, 0.02 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.504 \\,$ | $\\, 0.508 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.1 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5398 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5438 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5478 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5793 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5832 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5871 \\,$ |\n\nFor example, to determine the value of $\\Phi({\\color{red}0.12})$ from the table, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Select the row that corresponds to ${\\color{red}0.1}$ and the column that corresponds to $0.0{\\color{red}2}.$\n\n- Take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.01 \\,$ | $\\, 0.02 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.504 \\,$ | $\\, 0.508 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.1 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5398 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5438 \\,$ | $\\color{blue}\\, 0.5478 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5793 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5832 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5871 \\,$ |\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq 0.12) = \\Phi(0.12)=0.5478.\n$$\n\n**Note:** Since the function $f(z)$ is symmetric about the vertical axis and the total area under the curve must equal $1,$ we must have $\\Phi(0) = 0.5.$ This value is shown in the table.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-t8284\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n               \n                <div class=\"tutorial\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">The Standard Normal Cumulative Distribution Function</span></div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"t8284\">?</div>\n                    </div>                    \n    \n                    <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                    